  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Feedback Form Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is the feedback form?\", \"a\": \"A feedback form asks people to rate one experience and say what should change. It usually goes out right after a purchase or an appointment. Most pair a single rating, often 1 to 5 stars, with an optional comment box. The rating shows how it went, and the comment says why.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a feedback form?\", \"a\": \"Pick the decision the answers will inform, then write one rating question, one or two specific questions and a comment box. Choose when it goes out and who reads the low scores. Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a> turns that description into a working form with alerts and a database.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is another term for feedback form?\", \"a\": \"Comment card is the older name, from the paper slips left on restaurant tables. People also say evaluation form or feedback survey. A survey tends to run longer and go to a planned group, while a feedback form follows one specific experience.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are the different types of feedback forms?\", \"a\": \"The common split is by who answers. Customer and client feedback forms follow a purchase or a project. Talks and workshops get event forms. Clinics send one after each appointment. Inside a company, an employee feedback form asks staff about a manager or a process.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can you provide some examples of feedback forms?\", \"a\": \"A restaurant comment card asks about the food and the service. A post-delivery form asks for a star rating and what went wrong. Coaches send a coaching feedback form after each session to ask whether it moved the client toward a goal. When a review is glowing, a testimonial form asks permission to quote it.\"}, {\"q\": \"What questions should a feedback form include?\", \"a\": \"Open with one rating, such as how satisfied the person was with the visit. Add a question about the step you control, such as delivery speed. Close with an optional comment box. Good feedback form questions ask about one thing at a time and never two in one sentence.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a customer feedback form template include?\", \"a\": \"It should carry the order or visit it refers to, pulled from the link the customer clicked. Then add a satisfaction rating and a question about the reason. A simple feedback form with those parts plus an optional comment is quick to finish on a phone.\"}, {\"q\": \"What goes on an open house feedback form?\", \"a\": \"Ask visitors whether they work with an agent, what they think of the asking price and how the home compares with others they have toured. Other agents tour a listing before the public at a broker open house. That broker open house feedback form should focus on price and condition.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you make a feedback form for students?\", \"a\": \"Keep it to five questions about one course or unit, and let students answer without their names. Ask what helped them learn and what they would change. Teachers can collect it at the end of each unit. A training feedback form works the same way for adult learners.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a feedback form template in Word or PDF?\", \"a\": \"Word and PDF versions work on paper at a front desk or in a classroom. Someone then has to type every answer into a spreadsheet before anyone reads it. A star rating feedback form built online saves each answer as it arrives and alerts the right person to a low score.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
